{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01QAghc2nF9iRf4pVTNPVTTM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/06-007-real-time-vs-batch-processing-for-data-updates.md`** — Q7: Real-time vs batch processing for data updates.\n\nKey content:\n\n- **Decision axis: acceptable staleness** — maps SLA to architecture: sub-second → Kafka+Flink streaming; 1–60 min → micro-batch; hours/overnight → bulk Airflow batch\n- **Mechanism** — streaming exactly-once semantics vs batch simplicity; Lambda (batch correctness + streaming recency) vs Kappa (streaming-only replay) patterns\n- **RAG-specific pattern** — CDC via Debezium → Kafka → async embed worker → Pinecone upsert by `doc_id`, nightly full-sync for deletes, `index_lag_seconds` alert\n- **Feature store pattern** — online Redis (Kafka→Flink, sub-second reads for inference) + offline Parquet (nightly Spark for training)\n- **Pitfalls** — recommending Kafka by default without checking staleness tolerance; forgetting to handle deletes (ghost documents pollute retrieval); conflating Lambda and Kappa\n\nPlan updated and committed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":69401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4956db6a-6657-4657-afe2-0189f81f95a9","uuid":"d2d39c98-e8bf-4278-b39f-01afbe5de88f"}
